WEBVTT

00:01.210 --> 00:05.210
<b>Alright! So today, I was thinking we should
have a group discussion about justice.</b>

00:05.710 --> 00:10.000
<b>We're about to hit a turning point in our fight against
Evilus, so getting back to the basics couldn't hurt.</b>

00:10.210 --> 00:12.500
<b>I really don't think that's necessary...</b>

00:12.500 --> 00:14.000
<b>Oh c'mon, humor me!</b>

00:14.210 --> 00:16.420
<b>First, let's start off with what the word "justice" means.</b>

00:16.630 --> 00:17.920
<b>How would you define it?</b>

00:18.080 --> 00:19.580
<b>Define it...?</b>

00:20.710 --> 00:26.500
<b>"Good deeds done without the expectation of a reward in
return," i.e. "justice," would be the simplest way...</b>

00:26.750 --> 00:31.750
<b>Yeah, but if the good deeds don't serve a purpose,
then it's not any different than self-righteousness, is it?</b>

00:32.170 --> 00:38.500
<b>I disagree. If there's some sort of underlying goal,
then it's narcissism. And that's a far cry from real justice.</b>

00:39.000 --> 00:44.210
<b>When we raise the question of justice being "real" versus
"not real," we could probably argue about it forever...</b>

00:44.500 --> 00:49.460
<b>No. We pledged to uphold the Sword and Wings
of Justice. Our cause is more noble than-</b>

00:49.460 --> 00:51.790
<b>There she is! Lion the Armchair Philosopher!</b>

00:51.920 --> 00:54.290
<b>What do you mean, "armchair philosopher"?!</b>

00:54.460 --> 00:57.290
<b>Sorry, but I calls 'em like I sees 'em.</b>

00:57.880 --> 00:59.040
<b>Well, in my opinion...</b>

00:59.250 --> 01:04.130
<b>When all's said and done, concepts such
as justice are merely tools of convenience.</b>

01:04.630 --> 01:06.790
<b>A weapon used to justify a cause.</b>

01:07.130 --> 01:10.420
<b>A blank check written to warrant violence.</b>

01:10.540 --> 01:13.170
<b>Kaguya! Must you always be so cynical?</b>

01:13.170 --> 01:15.630
<b>Oh my, have I gotten something wrong?</b>

01:15.630 --> 01:18.460
<b>Yes, you have! Now take it back!</b>

01:18.830 --> 01:20.710
<b>Do you ever get tired of arguin'?</b>

01:39.170 --> 01:42.960
<b>Okay, I think that's enough discussion for one day!</b>

01:43.330 --> 01:48.920
<b>Even the gods have a tough time answering that one.
So there's no use losing sleep over it!</b>

01:49.670 --> 01:50.630
<b>What...?</b>

01:51.080 --> 01:55.920
<b>Anyone can wax poetic about justice.
And they can also abuse it for their own gain, right?</b>

01:56.380 --> 02:01.750
<b>So instead of trying to figure out the right answer,
let's focus on weeding out the phony kind of justice!</b>

02:02.540 --> 02:04.170
<b>The phony kind of justice...?</b>

02:04.420 --> 02:05.210
<b>That's right!</b>

02:05.330 --> 02:11.710
<b>Where fake justice withers away...
order, harmony, and happiness grow in its place!</b>

02:11.710 --> 02:16.170
<b>And THAT'S the kind of justice we,
the Astrea Familia, want most!</b>

02:17.130 --> 02:19.000
<b>We don't "bear the burden" of justice.</b>

02:19.460 --> 02:21.330
<b>'Cause if we did, it'd eventually squash us.</b>

02:21.750 --> 02:24.210
<b>And obviously it's not something we wield, either.</b>

02:24.630 --> 02:27.500
<b>That's practically guaranteed to be done in bad faith!</b>

02:29.420 --> 02:31.460
<b>Justice is something we hide.</b>

02:35.210 --> 02:38.460
<b>I see you've been stunned speechless
by my wisdom yet again!</b>

02:39.880 --> 02:41.290
<b>Nice going, me!</b>

02:43.670 --> 02:47.630
<b>She got everyone all riled up just
to pat herself on the back...</b>

02:49.420 --> 02:52.080
<b>What I wouldn't give to smack the smile off that face...</b>

03:07.750 --> 03:11.670
<b>Is it Wrong to Try to Pick Up Girls in a Dungeon?  IV</b>

04:27.000 --> 04:30.630
<b>Welf Crozzo</b>

04:27.000 --> 04:30.630
<b>Shikou</b>

04:27.420 --> 04:28.580
<b>Noah Heal...</b>

04:35.830 --> 04:36.830
<b>Thank goodness.</b>

04:37.330 --> 04:39.790
<b>But it isn't one hundred percent healed.</b>

04:42.080 --> 04:46.290
<b>Mr. Cranel, I still believe using my magic on you
would have been the better option.</b>

04:46.710 --> 04:49.040
<b>Thinking about it logically, that'd be a far more efficient-</b>

04:49.040 --> 04:51.210
<b>We've already been through this, Miss Ryu.</b>

04:51.630 --> 04:56.040
<b>Being able to walk on your own is more important,
and it makes things easier on me, too.</b>

04:56.460 --> 04:57.170
<b>Yes, but-</b>

04:59.000 --> 05:02.960
<b>Then we've reached an impasse.
We're both too stubborn to budge.</b>

05:06.250 --> 05:08.750
<b>Let's review the situation once more, shall we?</b>

05:09.130 --> 05:12.880
<b>Judging by our surroundings, we're on the 37th Floor...</b>

05:13.460 --> 05:16.040
<b>It seems that we are, without a doubt,
in the White Palace.</b>

05:16.250 --> 05:20.920
<b>However, I can't quite figure out
which area of the Floor we're in.</b>

05:21.580 --> 05:23.920
<b>In fact, it's unclear which direction we ought to go.</b>

05:24.830 --> 05:26.750
<b>We're lacking in both equipment and items.</b>

05:27.790 --> 05:32.830
<b>Should we persist in our journey and come up against
Deep Floor monsters, our chances are extremely slim.</b>

05:33.750 --> 05:37.170
<b>What's more, with the fatigue and
the number of injuries between us...</b>

05:37.960 --> 05:40.830
<b>We have no potions, nor a means of
receiving medical treatment.</b>

05:41.380 --> 05:46.880
<b>Until my Mind gives out, we're going to have to rely on
my healing magic as best we can.</b>

05:47.330 --> 05:51.290
<b>Would it be better to wait here
for someone to rescue us instead?</b>

05:52.790 --> 05:54.500
<b>I wouldn't get my hopes up.</b>

05:55.080 --> 05:58.170
<b>I can tell we're not anywhere near the normal route.</b>

05:58.790 --> 06:03.330
<b>This isn't the type of place that a Familia on an expedition
to the Deep Floors would just so happen find.</b>

06:03.920 --> 06:08.500
<b>And even if your friends were to catch wind
of our whereabouts, Mr. Cranel...</b>

06:08.830 --> 06:11.420
<b>there's no way they can make it here by themselves.</b>

06:13.380 --> 06:14.380
<b>I guess you're right...</b>

06:15.330 --> 06:21.500
<b>Besides, until the chaos on the 27th Floor subsides,
no one will volunteer to look for us.</b>

06:21.500 --> 06:23.500
<b>Even if they put out a search quest.</b>

06:24.710 --> 06:28.330
<b>So if we stay here... eventually,
we'll just end up like them.</b>

06:33.880 --> 06:38.790
<b>No matter what happens, don't let any monsters
get close to Master Welf! Is that clear?!</b>

06:57.580 --> 06:58.580
<b>Here goes nothin'.</b>

07:05.040 --> 07:07.920
<b>Forging weapons in the Dungeon?
The man's got a screw loose.</b>

07:08.830 --> 07:11.000
<b>If those monsters realize we're hidin' back here...</b>

07:11.210 --> 07:13.500
<b>It's too late to chicken out now, Bors.</b>

07:13.790 --> 07:18.750
<b>I know! But even if the blacksmith DOES manage to
make a blade, it ain't gonna do us any-</b>

07:18.750 --> 07:19.830
<b>We must have faith in him!</b>

07:20.830 --> 07:25.130
<b>He's risking his life to forge that sword,
so we'll use it to get out of this mess!</b>

07:26.830 --> 07:28.710
<b>It's our only chance at survival...</b>

07:28.790 --> 07:31.920
<b>Our one and only chance at saving Master Bell!</b>

07:32.250 --> 07:34.170
<b>We all gotta die sometime, don't we?</b>

07:34.380 --> 07:38.420
<b>If you wanna make it back home,
I suggest you hold on tight to that shield.</b>

07:41.250 --> 07:43.960
<b>Rabbit Foot's friends are all lunatics, I swear!</b>

07:49.580 --> 07:50.330
<b>They found us!</b>

07:53.420 --> 07:54.670
<b>Hell Kaios!</b>

08:00.460 --> 08:02.290
<b>Screw it, make the stupid sword!</b>

08:35.420 --> 08:37.670
<b>You don't have to kill 'em! Just cut off their legs!</b>

08:40.250 --> 08:41.960
<b>I don't even have time to aim!</b>

08:52.040 --> 08:52.880
<b>Dammit...</b>

08:53.210 --> 08:56.290
<b>THIS is what Adamantite's like?! Gimme a break!</b>

08:57.130 --> 08:58.920
<b>Am I not strong enough to shape this stuff?!</b>

09:02.040 --> 09:03.710
<b>In light of our current situation,</b>

09:04.290 --> 09:09.420
<b>we should head for the tunnel that leads up
to the 36th Floor once we get out of here.</b>

09:10.080 --> 09:13.380
<b>The 36th Floor... So, the Lower Floors?</b>

09:13.710 --> 09:18.170
<b>Right. The Deep Floors' first safety point isn't until the
39th Floor.</b>

09:18.960 --> 09:22.710
<b>Climbing down two floors in order to reach a safety point
would be a far more difficult endeavor.</b>

09:24.040 --> 09:27.170
<b>Of course, even if we make it there,
we won't necessarily be safe.</b>

09:28.000 --> 09:32.170
<b>But at least the Lower Floors have
water, nuts, and berries. Fruit, too.</b>

09:32.630 --> 09:34.710
<b>That gives us a much higher chance of survival.</b>

09:36.580 --> 09:42.380
<b>I guess you might say the Lower Floors will be a little
more kind to us... compared to the Deep Floors.</b>

09:44.960 --> 09:49.210
<b>But we're not entirely sure how to get to
the connecting tunnel from here, are we?</b>

09:49.750 --> 09:53.540
<b>No. And the journey will probably be an unpleasant one.</b>

09:54.170 --> 09:58.500
<b>From here on out, each of our choices could
mean the difference between life and death.</b>

09:58.790 --> 10:04.040
<b>We'll have to use my magic sparingly...
We'll try to save it for when death is the only alternative.</b>

10:04.500 --> 10:05.210
<b>Got it...</b>

10:05.920 --> 10:11.830
<b>And unfortunately... if we're going to traverse this Floor,
we'll need to procure more items and equipment.</b>

10:12.750 --> 10:14.670
<b>And water, if possible...</b>

10:15.330 --> 10:16.960
<b>But where would we-</b>

10:18.290 --> 10:18.960
<b>Miss Ryu?</b>

10:19.130 --> 10:21.000
<b>We have to strip them of their gear.</b>

10:28.630 --> 10:30.500
<b>What are you talking about, Miss Ryu?!</b>

10:31.000 --> 10:35.540
<b>We're going to strip the corpses of their gear
and take what we need for our own use.</b>

10:35.830 --> 10:38.880
<b>W-wait a minute! We'd be desecrating their bodies-</b>

10:38.880 --> 10:43.960
<b>We're putting fellow adventurers slain by the Dungeon
to good use. We don't have a choice in the matter.</b>

10:45.920 --> 10:49.420
<b>I'll search the woman. Mr. Cranel, you take the men.</b>

11:09.540 --> 11:13.710
<b>Of course. Miss Ryu... For a noble Elf like her...</b>

11:14.250 --> 11:16.630
<b>There's no way this isn't killing her inside.</b>

11:17.130 --> 11:19.790
<b>She's doing it to survive... Doing it for me...</b>

11:23.380 --> 11:26.880
<b>I'm so sorry... I want to make it home in one piece!</b>

11:32.710 --> 11:35.210
<b>This is the Dungeon.</b>

11:36.250 --> 11:38.330
<b>This is what it means to be an adventurer.</b>

11:40.210 --> 11:43.420
<b>Anything I say now is just an attempt
to rationalize my actions...</b>

11:44.630 --> 11:47.000
<b>But please, let me say it anyway.</b>

11:47.630 --> 11:50.290
<b>I'm going to live life enough for all of you.</b>

11:50.920 --> 11:52.670
<b>I can't ask for your forgiveness...</b>

11:53.380 --> 11:59.500
<b>But because of you, with your help,
I know that we can escape from the Deep Floors!</b>

12:01.630 --> 12:04.790
<b>I swear, we WILL make it back to the surface.</b>

12:06.920 --> 12:08.420
<b>I think that's about everything.</b>

12:08.920 --> 12:09.750
<b>Yeah...</b>

12:10.040 --> 12:12.540
<b>Our most valuable discovery... might be this.</b>

12:13.540 --> 12:15.040
<b>Is that a map...?</b>

12:15.330 --> 12:21.330
<b>Yes. It's incomplete, but it covers a fairly large distance,
and it depicts the details of the surrounding area.</b>

12:22.460 --> 12:28.460
<b>I can't even imagine how hopeless they must have felt...
but it's going to be a huge help to us.</b>

12:29.040 --> 12:33.080
<b>If we know which routes are dead ends,
then we won't have to scope them out for ourselves.</b>

12:33.080 --> 12:34.380
<b>That's a good point.</b>

12:35.130 --> 12:37.250
<b>So if this is the room we're in right now...</b>

12:37.540 --> 12:41.580
<b>...do you have any idea which part
of the Floor this maze is on?</b>

12:42.170 --> 12:45.380
<b>No. The 37th Floor is massive.</b>

12:46.040 --> 12:48.250
<b>It runs almost as wide as the whole of Orario.</b>

12:48.960 --> 12:52.830
<b>I don't recognize the area shown on the map, anyway.</b>

12:53.380 --> 12:59.330
<b>That being said, I've been to the Deep Floors countless
times. I remember what the normal route looks like.</b>

12:59.670 --> 13:00.540
<b>Then...?</b>

13:00.540 --> 13:06.830
<b>Precisely. If we follow the map and use it to guide
ourselves back to the Dungeon's normal route, then...</b>

13:07.830 --> 13:09.960
<b>...I can lead us to the connecting tunnel.</b>

13:11.330 --> 13:12.790
<b>It seems we have our heading.</b>

13:13.040 --> 13:13.790
<b>Yeah!</b>

13:14.130 --> 13:16.080
<b>I don't know what we're going to need.</b>

13:16.380 --> 13:19.000
<b>Let's bring as much of their gear as we can carry.</b>

13:30.330 --> 13:31.580
<b>Is something the matter?</b>

13:31.580 --> 13:37.080
<b>No, it's just that they still had food on them...
So I can't help but wonder why they didn't make it.</b>

13:37.670 --> 13:40.040
<b>And it's not like they ran out of potions...</b>

13:41.210 --> 13:44.080
<b>They might have been poisoned by monsters.</b>

13:44.630 --> 13:45.540
<b>Oh...</b>

13:46.920 --> 13:48.080
<b>There aren't any antidotes in here!</b>

13:48.630 --> 13:53.500
<b>I suspect they used this room as a base while
they were searching for a safe path home...</b>

13:54.580 --> 13:57.130
<b>...but they ended up exhausting their supply of antidotes.</b>

13:57.630 --> 14:01.250
<b>The poison spread through their bodies,
and once these two could no longer move...</b>

14:01.250 --> 14:03.710
<b>they pinned their hopes on their remaining friend.</b>

14:04.210 --> 14:06.420
<b>But their friend couldn't do it either...</b>

14:07.210 --> 14:10.130
<b>He couldn't handle the darkness
of the Deep Floors on his own...</b>

14:13.290 --> 14:14.290
<b>Mr. Cranel.</b>

14:17.000 --> 14:19.670
<b>Is that a Familia emblem...?</b>

14:19.670 --> 14:24.750
<b>Indeed. I can't quite make it out, but...
these guys were desperate.</b>

14:24.750 --> 14:27.920
<b>They probably didn't have anything
else to draw the map on.</b>

14:36.040 --> 14:37.330
<b>There's something written here!</b>

14:37.830 --> 14:46.540
<b>"Forgive us, my god... re...
Sorry, Mom... not coming home..."</b>

14:49.630 --> 14:53.250
<b>Miss Ryu, let's bring this banner back
to the surface with us!</b>

14:53.830 --> 14:56.080
<b>We have to make it home, for them!</b>

15:24.500 --> 15:27.460
<b>What the hell am I doing...? We don't have time for this!</b>

15:28.000 --> 15:31.330
<b>I'm supposed to be forging
a gods-damned magic sword over here!</b>

15:48.960 --> 15:54.250
<b>Maybe it WAS a dumb idea,
crafting a weapon in the Dungeon...</b>

15:54.670 --> 15:58.500
<b>Did I overestimate myself? Did I just want
to be the first person who's ever done it?</b>

15:59.500 --> 16:03.920
<b>Did I promise something I can't deliver and
make my closest friends stake their lives on it?!</b>

16:04.920 --> 16:08.540
<b>Let me ask you again: Is your fire burning bright?</b>

16:08.830 --> 16:11.790
<b>Oh it's burning, alright... Hotter than the frickin' Sun!</b>

16:12.210 --> 16:17.000
<b>I'm pouring all of my strength, all of my skills,
all of my pride as a blacksmith into it!</b>

16:17.460 --> 16:18.330
<b>And yet-</b>

16:18.330 --> 16:19.420
<b>You sure about that?</b>

16:21.130 --> 16:22.920
<b>Remember what your family used to say:</b>

16:23.290 --> 16:29.130
<b>"Listen to the metal's voice, let its sound ring in your ears,
and then put your soul into your hammer."</b>

16:29.500 --> 16:31.880
<b>Shut up! To hell with the Crozzo family!</b>

16:32.540 --> 16:35.250
<b>All I care about right now is finishing this stupid sword!</b>

16:35.580 --> 16:36.750
<b>Why's that?</b>

16:38.210 --> 16:40.380
<b>Why are you swinging your hammer?</b>

16:40.380 --> 16:41.580
<b>To craft a weapon!</b>

16:42.670 --> 16:44.830
<b>Okay, then why are you crafting a weapon?</b>

16:45.000 --> 16:46.210
<b>To survive!</b>

16:46.210 --> 16:48.960
<b>Wrong. That's not what I asked.</b>

16:49.580 --> 16:51.330
<b>Look deep inside yourself.</b>

16:51.920 --> 16:53.420
<b>And no cop-out answers, either.</b>

16:54.210 --> 16:57.170
<b>Who are you crafting these weapons FOR?</b>

17:02.380 --> 17:05.380
<b>Do everything you can to hold them off
until Master Welf's done forging the blade!</b>

17:05.380 --> 17:06.630
<b>Yeah, I get it!</b>

17:12.080 --> 17:13.080
<b>You guys...</b>

17:14.500 --> 17:16.080
<b>One last question:</b>

17:16.420 --> 17:19.250
<b>Why are you so bent on doing this?</b>

17:21.880 --> 17:23.830
<b>It's for... my friends...</b>

17:24.670 --> 17:25.500
<b>That's right...</b>

17:26.460 --> 17:30.210
<b>How could I have forgotten
something so painfully obvious?</b>

17:31.290 --> 17:35.460
<b>"Why do I craft weapons?" I do it for Bell, for my friends!</b>

17:51.580 --> 17:53.420
<b>We might actually pull this off...!</b>

17:53.420 --> 17:57.630
<b>Shit, I dunno what changed,
but I'm startin' to get a second wind!</b>

17:59.670 --> 18:01.630
<b>Yeah, I see it now.</b>

18:01.630 --> 18:05.500
<b>It doesn't matter how powerful they are...
An ordinary magic sword isn't gonna cut it!</b>

18:06.460 --> 18:08.000
<b>A magic sword is guaranteed to break!</b>

18:08.420 --> 18:10.080
<b>Eventually, its wielder HAS to say goodbye!</b>

18:10.540 --> 18:14.080
<b>So all I have to do... is forge a blade to beats all blades!</b>

18:14.920 --> 18:17.420
<b>An indestructible magic sword!</b>

18:18.750 --> 18:22.130
<b>Then should I assume Tsubaki
went down into the Dungeon, too?</b>

18:22.460 --> 18:25.920
<b>Uh-huh. Naza and Miach were
the ones who approached her.</b>

18:26.500 --> 18:29.290
<b>And honestly, we're grateful for all the help we can get...</b>

18:29.750 --> 18:32.500
<b>Well... it is what it is, I suppose.</b>

18:32.830 --> 18:38.080
<b>It was an urgent situation. Even if I'd tried to stop her,
Tsubaki probably would have gone anyway.</b>

18:38.750 --> 18:40.880
<b>And? What was the other thing?</b>

18:41.040 --> 18:43.330
<b>Oh, uh, about that...</b>

18:45.210 --> 18:51.000
<b>Expeditions cost an awful lot of money! So wouldja mind
if we skip the payment for Bell's knife this month?</b>

18:51.000 --> 18:51.920
<b>Not happening.</b>

18:51.920 --> 18:52.580
<b>Seriously?!</b>

18:52.580 --> 18:53.580
<b>But why?!</b>

18:54.460 --> 18:55.880
<b>You know why, Hestia.</b>

18:56.670 --> 19:00.880
<b>I have no doubt that knife has saved
the boy's life countless times by now.</b>

19:03.880 --> 19:07.880
<b>Don't you care about him? Is his life worth so little to you?</b>

19:07.880 --> 19:10.000
<b>O-of course I care about him!</b>

19:10.630 --> 19:12.080
<b>Then cough up the cash.</b>

19:12.420 --> 19:15.500
<b>Prove that you're still willing to do
whatever it takes to protect him.</b>

19:24.000 --> 19:26.750
<b>That's it, I need a blade with divine power!</b>

19:27.170 --> 19:29.460
<b>Like the one that she... that the goddess made.</b>

19:29.630 --> 19:31.130
<b>A weapon of the highest caliber!</b>

19:35.170 --> 19:38.460
<b>Hang in there, Bell... I'm not gonna turn my back on you!</b>

19:38.920 --> 19:40.460
<b>We'll walk side by side!</b>

19:41.000 --> 19:45.630
<b>In fact... if you're not careful, I might even
leave you and Lady Hephaistos in the dust!</b>

19:46.040 --> 19:48.670
<b>Get ready, 'cause... HERE I COME!</b>

19:56.710 --> 19:57.460
<b>Oh crap!</b>

19:57.460 --> 19:58.250
<b>Ouka!</b>

20:07.210 --> 20:09.330
<b>It's about time, blacksmith...</b>

20:21.540 --> 20:22.790
<b>Sorry for the wait.</b>

20:25.630 --> 20:27.630
<b>H-hey! What do we do now?!</b>

20:27.790 --> 20:29.080
<b>Master Welf!</b>

20:29.330 --> 20:32.420
<b>My magic alone won't be enough.
Can you lend me a hand?</b>

20:32.420 --> 20:33.960
<b>Huh? Oh, okay!</b>

20:37.380 --> 20:39.170
<b>Now the real test begins!</b>

20:43.460 --> 20:45.540
<b>Shikou... KAZUKI!</b>

21:16.630 --> 21:17.580
<b>Master Welf...</b>

21:18.500 --> 21:20.170
<b>Yup, it's all done.</b>

21:22.630 --> 21:29.040
<b>A shatterproof magic sword. The blade and its wielder
work hand in hand... standing by each other for life.</b>

21:39.500 --> 21:43.460
<b>That's what the last part of the prophecy
meant by "the great daystar's golden rays"!</b>

21:45.290 --> 21:46.380
<b>This is the beginning.</b>

21:47.210 --> 21:50.380
<b>The first step of my journey
to take my skills to new heights!</b>

21:53.330 --> 21:56.460
<b>You put your lives in my hands. Now I'm giving 'em back.</b>

21:58.750 --> 22:01.040
<b>Gear up! It's time to go find Bell!</b>

22:01.540 --> 22:02.920
<b>Yeah!</b>

23:35.040 --> 23:40.040
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.040 --> 23:40.040
<b>White Palace</b>

23:35.040 --> 23:40.040
<b>White Labyrinth</b>

23:36.250 --> 23:38.630
<b>Next time: "White Palace."</b>
